In article <woolto_c.747630261@kultarr> woolto_c@cs.uwa.oz.au (Zodiac) writes:

>I'm trying to teach my older brother how to play, but I'm not telling him too
>much, just helping him to understand how the game works etc.
>...
>So I say to him "You wanna try to stay satiated so that you don't run out of
>food.  Learn what corpses are safe to eat, and eat them if you're not satiated.
>But don't eat when you're satiated because you can choke and die."

Bad idea, for three reasons.

1) You can accidentally choke and die if you aren't careful,
   as your brother did on a dead snake.

2) Even if you are careful, you may occasionally kill something
   that you want to eat _right away_ to gain intrinsics, levels,
   or stats.  Unless you can teleport and have teleport control,
   you can't get rid of the food in your stomach fast enough
   before the corpse decomposes.  (Unless you have an ice box or
   tinning kit, but they're fairly rare _and_ heavy.)

3) Being in the satiated state reduces your chances of increasing
   your dexterity ("You feel limber!") and increases your chances
   of reducing your dexterity ("You feel clumsy!").


