In many articles <blah-blah-blah>, people write:

> [Floating eyes kill me all the time when I run down hallways]

How does this happen to you people?  On my versions (3.1.3 on a Sparc 2
or 3.1.1 on an Apollo), when you use Shift-[hjkl] to run down hallways,
you do not bash monsters when you encounter them; you stop.  If you want
to be extra safe, use Ctrl-[hjkl], and you don't walk past or into doorways
or traps.  Are you "running" by holding down [hjkl]???

Another tip for dealing with eyes:  If you don't have a missile weapon,
*DON'T* say, "What the heck, maybe I'll get lucky if I just beat on him."
Instead, lure it into a large room (it follows you, slowly), and throw
your weapons at it until it dies or until you run out of weapons
(you can decide yourself if you want to risk throwing your primary weapon).
It will eventually move, you can go pick up your weapons, and repeat
until it dies.

